  "result": "Shell completion now handles arguments that contain `#` correctly in bash, zsh, fish and PowerShell. The full test suite passes (1913 passed, 102 skipped), and the 7 new tests fail when the fix is taken out.\n\n**Cause:** completion splits the command line with Python's `shlex`, which treats an unquoted `#` as the start of a comment. Everything from the `#` onward was dropped, so completion saw a shorter command line. In fish this could also crash with an `IndexError`.\n\n**Fix:** one line in `split_arg_string` (`src/click/shell_completion.py`) that tells `shlex` not to treat `#` as a comment.\n\n**Also changed:**\n- **`tests/test_parser.py`:** three new splitting cases: `cli #foo`, `cli a # b` and `cli a#b`.\n- **`tests/test_shell_completion.py`:** a new test, `test_full_complete_hash`, that runs completion end to end for all four shells, with `#` in both an earlier argument and the word being completed.\n- **`CHANGES.md`:** 8.5.0 is already released, so I added a new \"Version 8.5.1 \u2013 Unreleased\" section for the entry. I also added a matching `versionchanged:: 8.5.1` note to the function's docstring. Adjust the version if the next release will be numbered differently.\n\nNothing is committed yet.",
